  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "present simple: be (am/is/are) with age",
      "title_form": "El verbo ser/estar con la edad",
      "title_target": "The verb to be with age",
      "description_md_form": "Para hablar de la edad en inglés, usamos el verbo **to be** (ser/estar), no el verbo *tener* como en español. La estructura es: **sujeto + am/is/are + número + years old**.\n\n- **I am** seven years old. (Tengo siete años.)\n- **She is** nine years old. (Ella tiene nueve años.)\n\nLa forma del verbo cambia según el sujeto:\n\n| Sujeto | Forma |\n|--------|-------|\n| I | am |\n| he/she/it | is |\n| you/we/they | are |\n\nPara preguntar, usamos **How old are you?** (¿Cuántos años tienes?).",
      "description_md_target": "To talk about age in English, we use the verb **to be**, not the verb *to have* as in Spanish. The structure is: **subject + am/is/are + number + years old**.\n\n- **I am** seven years old.\n- **She is** nine years old.\n\nThe form of the verb changes with the subject:\n\n| Subject | Form |\n|---------|------|\n| I | am |\n| he/she/it | is |\n| you/we/they | are |\n\nTo ask, we use **How old are you?**",
      "grammar_structure": "Subject + am/is/are + number + years old",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "present_simple_be",
        "headers": [
          "Pronombre",
          "Forma",
          "Ejemplo"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "I",
            "am",
            "I am seven years old."
          ],
          [
            "you",
            "are",
            "You are nine years old."
          ],
          [
            "he/she/it",
            "is",
            "She is five years old."
          ],
          [
            "we",
            "are",
            "We are ten years old."
          ],
          [
            "they",
            "are",
            "They are eight years old."
          ]
        ]
      },
